{"title":"2025 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:15)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:15)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Chinese_Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Chinese Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(In_2_Mins)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (In 2 Mins)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the unique positive integer such that dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb7388ce9f5d0542c2d8ea4a4ce22925d1d96e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273436$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> leaves a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b74c71559f14bd3b12ba3b1c7bbe2cba2bc203.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272760$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> leaves a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the tens digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/790fd2f1643b47466e5d327bc932fe70d7503210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"355\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The problem statement implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> divides both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04d483fbf94aadbd4ffc6b74038319d1a653e0fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273436-16=273420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"176\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee874ef0cdd452a6711606d4a9764aae4833c0bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272760-15=272745$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"176\" height=\"15\" />. We want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b08165cfb14f091401e2d4d2cf48180c1deae3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N &gt; 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> that satisfies both of these conditions. \nHence, we can just find the greatest common divisor of the two numbers. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/68070a5fba41d8acbdb3da0aaf9733d03d42f0c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(273420,272745)=\\gcd(675,272745)=\\gcd(675,45)=\\gcd(0,45)=45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"579\" height=\"20\" /> by the Euclidean Algorithm, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c633a2ad3e960a8f9b7aac769ce5eb523bd08119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E) }4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>Note: If an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is congruent to an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> modulo a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8c5bc2f80ebae1920268e3e1d48432781854257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv b \\pmod{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"20\" />, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> divides the difference, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/3311eba472bf7dc846f58d649d3756cf443eb108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a-b|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> (Euclidean Algorithm)\n</p><p>~Tacos_are_yummy_1\n</p><p>~andliu766\n</p><p>minor edits by AD_12 and mw2014\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/164896eb2b8f5defc78df01680a71d7fc928668d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273436 \\equiv 16 \\pmod N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be2f57083709e35c220888057c5a431217c08b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272760 \\equiv 15 \\pmod N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />, from which we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a1ab0bdbf425e2371ee52594c4aff71d8a42df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420 \\equiv 0 \\pmod N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/c/62c8b5975c9ea9e82ce29dc41d171da90c6561bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272745 \\equiv 0 \\pmod N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Substracting the two gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/4/f041c4da37d32ca03eff1d3f6b19b62301f39c7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420 - 272745 = 675$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"185\" height=\"15\" />, which is also divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the only possible divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c44aa4857623b789be4bcc7b0b048c00e3900ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$675$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a556ae9befd6a0b57142d7b23d6df3802de1cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25, 27, 45, 75, 135, 225,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c44aa4857623b789be4bcc7b0b048c00e3900ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$675$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Checking which ones also divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb7388ce9f5d0542c2d8ea4a4ce22925d1d96e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273436$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debae0d977b575f0bf43f2acf1ef4cf60687823f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> eliminates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/0/f3006029c3e142b1baf2a25b3f8cfd99e5c37544.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420 \\equiv 0 \\pmod {45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Since both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debae0d977b575f0bf43f2acf1ef4cf60687823f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c44aa4857623b789be4bcc7b0b048c00e3900ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$675$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f14c18e94260093ec27dba4695bf85cc87cfc0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420-675=272745$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"185\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be5fd97cc911ec81deb96a67db99ad6b0c1fa572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> works, and its tens digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b4198920681ecb231a4fd1c42717a4272ee37de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"50\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Continuous_Pi\n</p><p>~edited by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Zhixing\" title=\"User:Zhixing\">Zhixing</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We get that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58f6dad2d3be060d0220c1b9b8fa30a58a1c7432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273436 \\equiv {16}\\pmod{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81e5f8b54a5abf91edff491c0ad9046c962fe57f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272760 \\equiv {15}\\pmod{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>So we also have that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/0/c5001f7fc07eed3f0455075fef6c2ba8aa8b5fdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420 \\equiv {0}\\pmod{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"20\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8f83e129158e8a314f2bf5350282fb56d5be82e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272745 \\equiv {0}\\pmod{N}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Notice that these are a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Now, we subtract these numbers to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c44aa4857623b789be4bcc7b0b048c00e3900ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$675$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\nWe see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a246e891c12fbba861b71440fff18c6e678b5f4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$675 = 25 \\cdot 27.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" /> There is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debae0d977b575f0bf43f2acf1ef4cf60687823f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4679ffdad99e77049767f510aa03986a9339ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272745$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> are multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as well, so our answer is just 45. Now the ten's digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b4198920681ecb231a4fd1c42717a4272ee37de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"50\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Aarav22\n</p><p>~reformatting by Alzwang\n</p><p>~minor editing by kfclover\n</p><p>~minor editing by Meoweashan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52da7d27b51994c369fd8b9517b4c12d11e88454.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273436 \\equiv 16 \\pmod{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3c722e03b6090c7b66fdabef8ba86ff8edae9d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272760 \\equiv 15 \\pmod{N}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />  \nSubtracting, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a3d72e866d4983a89eab444d656663e46e28e84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273436 - 272760 = 676 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{N}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"303\" height=\"20\" />  \n</p><p>This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/72546521a8538ce004cf93e803ab2130d7b7c7ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$675.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />  \nAlso, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1bbf5e948f301df1fd1681076ca091fbf032ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273436 \\equiv 16 \\pmod{N},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9dcaf28b2e929e0e23103a79b57698916ee36b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{N}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />  \n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> divides both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debae0d977b575f0bf43f2acf1ef4cf60687823f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/72546521a8538ce004cf93e803ab2130d7b7c7ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$675.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> Using the Euclidean Algorithm:  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/1/451923a6aea567165bc1054ebad7fe658fbf3c5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420 - 405 \\times 675 = 45,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"203\" height=\"17\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/b/3eb6e932f5a09aa87f24962f7ff13f249091ceee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(273420, 675) = 45.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" />  \n</p><p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c9852ff2188b0fc17576e888b8b840e26f10d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 45,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> and the tens digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c633a2ad3e960a8f9b7aac769ce5eb523bd08119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E) }4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~samma\n~minor LaTeX edits by vinceS\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This way is not that intelligent, but it's not that tedious or terrible. \n</p><p>If dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb7388ce9f5d0542c2d8ea4a4ce22925d1d96e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273436$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> gets a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04d483fbf94aadbd4ffc6b74038319d1a653e0fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273436-16=273420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"176\" height=\"15\" />. Similarly, if dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b74c71559f14bd3b12ba3b1c7bbe2cba2bc203.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272760$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> gets a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4679ffdad99e77049767f510aa03986a9339ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272745$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Also note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> to be a valid remainder when dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we can factorize these two numbers that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must be a factor of and see where it gets us.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debae0d977b575f0bf43f2acf1ef4cf60687823f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> is obviously a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because it ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so long division gets us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dab0bc0cb3dcf8e0fcb67a1d5d11521fc7423d7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420 = 13671 \\cdot 20 = 13671 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"272\" height=\"14\" />. Since the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4ad3fd38c618b38173294a6d1adddce15505bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13671$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, it must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we can divide it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/205900325bbe4640fee030d7e77214e600441cb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13671 = 9 \\cdot 1519$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/f/5cf258610e68285eacd1b1d457c2aeab9c7134e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$273420 = 4 \\cdot 1519 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"184\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31e31a15baa85f80aad6c89592f81b5401392809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1519$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> doesn't look that nice to factor immediately, so we can leave it like that for now. \n</p><p>We can do a similar thing for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4679ffdad99e77049767f510aa03986a9339ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$272745$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> to get that it equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3c0ede78bcb4d5af7e18e0139998fdd074365e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 30305 = 9 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 6061$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Now, we need to find a common factor between these two that's also greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Immediately, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/b/d4b493cb9af08d90570e8f66ab142dbd9d915b95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 5 = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> works. Since the problem says <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is unique, or even just that we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> already works, we can stop here. \n</p><p>However, if for some reason you weren't reading carefully or your brain stopped braining and tried to find the highest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, you would have checked if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31e31a15baa85f80aad6c89592f81b5401392809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1519$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/f/0ef3a781c4669441ed607194468eafda678523e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6061$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> share any common factors that would increase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. The Euclidean Algorithm shows that their <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/5967c0096e6595ca1e47d71f5ebfbc47d8516ae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> still is the only solution. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b4198920681ecb231a4fd1c42717a4272ee37de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"50\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p>~vaishnav\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E1:15.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:15)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:15)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:15)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/hDIe9NEYvxA\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/hDIe9NEYvxA</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_rufRRiCGKE\">https://youtu.be/_rufRRiCGKE</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Easy)\">Video Solution(Quick and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https: